1
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:36,000
Girl in the Basement is a thriller, crime, tv movie
film directed by Elisabeth Röhm.

2
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Sara is a teen girl who is looking forward to her 18th birthday
to move away from her controlling father Don.

3
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:36,000
But before she could even blow out the candles, Don
imprisons her in the basement of their home.

4
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Don, played by Judd Nelson.

5
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:36,000
Sara, played by Stefanie Scott.

6
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:06,000
Irene, played by Joely Fisher.

7
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:36,000
Michael, played by Braxton Bjerken.

8
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Doctor, played by Kim Rosen.

9
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
Amy, played by Emily Topper.

10
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Elisabeth Röhm ( "Rame" or  "rem"; German: [ˈʁøːm]; born April 28, 1973)
is an American television and film actress and director.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
She is best known for playing Kate Lockley in the television series Angel from 1999 to 2001
and Serena Southerlyn in the television series Law & Order from 2001 to 2005.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
She has also appeared in films such as Miss Congeniality 2: Armed and Fabulous (2005), American Hustle (2013), Joy (2015),
Seduced (2016), Once Upon a Time in Venice (2017), The Tribes of Palos Verdes (2017) and Bombshell (2019).

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Röhm made her directorial debut with the Lifetime
film Girl in the Basement (2021).

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film explores themes of imprisonment, based on true
story, basement, controlling parent.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The tone is intense.
